\f0\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
uthor one expert-level, numeric-graded genomics analysis problem. The cards below run in authoring order, and together they are the scientific case report that ships with the task.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa79\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Classification.
\f0\b0 \'a0Set the Genomics Domain, Subdomain, and the number of Decision Points. Minimum 5.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Prompt.
\f0\b0 \'a0Write the minimal viable prompt (question + estimand + exact JSON answer schema). Name the staged files by bare filename and tell the agent to write its final answer to eval_answer.json. Do not prescribe the method.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Setup & Environment.
\f0\b0 \'a0Describe the scenario you staged and declare the runtime the agent gets. Verify what the container actually provides before you declare it, and do not assume any third-party library is present. There is no R, no PLINK, no bedtools, no browser and no web access.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Staged data files.
\f0\b0 \'a0Upload the task's simulated data files with the Task Input Files card below. They mount flat at /filesystem/, which is the working directory for the code-execution tool. There is no subdirectory and you cannot create one. The prompt 'Upload to context' button does NOT reach the sandbox. In the prompt, name files by bare filename, never by directory.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Data Generation & Grounding.
\f0\b0 \'a0Define your symbols in Variables & Assumptions, keeping the latent generating variables separate from what the agent can recover from the released files. Fill the Data Generation Spec, paste the Generator Script, pin the Generator Seed, and list every staged file in the Data File Manifest. Then ground every biological parameter in References with a DOI or PMID and the published range it sits in. A graded value no citation supports does not ship.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Estimand & Estimator.
\f0\b0 \'a0State the target formally, and say plainly that the graded number is the finite-sample estimate recoverable from the staged files, not the parameter you seeded. Then give the reference estimator stage by stage, together with the defensible variants that still land inside tolerance.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Grader contract.
\f0\b0 \'a0Fill Answer Schema, Ground Truth, Tolerances, and the Reward Logic that says how the criteria combine into a score.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Golden Response.
\f0\b0 \'a0The Structure Diagram (the reference path plus each shortcut branch annotated with the value it returns), and the Solution Process (stage-by-stage walkthrough naming the method and the value each stage recovers).\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Decision Points & Reproducible Validation.
\f0\b0 \'a0Fill the Ablation Table: one row per analysis path with its output, absolute error, multiples of tolerance, pass or fail, and the stage that breaks. Include the reference row and every variant that legitimately passes, not only the failures. Then record Reproduction Evidence.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Rubric.
\f0\b0 \'a0Read the Rubric card description before you start; the requirements changed. You need the composite GENEBENCH BINARY row as your first criterion, then one wrong-path landmark AND one weighted reasoning criterion per decision point, plus a Schema Contract and one numeric check per graded key.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	11	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
QC & Contamination.
\f0\b0 \'a0Record the sample-QC decisions the answer depends on, and whether the scenario or answer is reachable in public sources.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	12	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Run Models / Grades.
\f0\b0 \'a0Run the three models; the numeric grader marks each field against the ground truth within tolerance.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

