\cf5 \cb3 ## Stage 0 (data quality)\cf0 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb3 - Blank / NA-like strings and JSON `null` become `null`. **Do not impute.**\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Drop a row only when **every** feature is null after that step.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Parse `diagnosis_datetime` and `ngs_datetime` to UTC ISO-8601; unparsable 
\f7 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  `null`.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - If a column is all-null on retained rows, drop it (`dropped_column`).\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Missing counts are taken **before** row drop.\cf0 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb3 ## Aim 1 statistics\cf0 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb3 - Prevalence and prevalence ratio (brain mets / no brain mets) for gene mutations and pathways.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Top 10 genes and all 10 pathways, ranked by mutated brain-met count (ties: name).\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Pairwise Pearson r on numeric fields (pairwise complete).\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - For each top-10 gene: highest-`|r|` pathway (signed r) and univariate logistic OR for `any_brain_met`.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Univariate logistic (IRLS) with Wald p and BH q (within genes vs within pathways).\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 - Fisher's exact, Holm, Katz CI, and multivariate logistic on 1 gene + 4 pathways.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 - Metadata filled as a JSON dataset (template fields, checksums, no-imputation strategy).\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
